 "brief": "Disease cases including diarrhea, cramps, rash, fever and hepatitis A are persistent in displacement camps throughout Gaza, the Shehab Wire reported. The Health Ministry documents new cases daily linked to absorption wells and makeshift water tanks operating without sanitation standards across the territory.\n\nHealth authorities attribute the outbreak pattern to contaminated water infrastructure serving the displaced population. Hepatitis A and gastrointestinal illnesses represent the primary health threat in camp conditions where water systems lack proper regulation and maintenance.",
